.SH "React + TypeScript + Vite"
.PP
This template provides a minimal setup to get React working in Vite with HMR and some ESLint rules\&.

.PP
Currently, two official plugins are available:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR@vitejs/plugin-react\fP uses \fRBabel\fP (or \fRoxc\fP when used in \fRrolldown-vite\fP) for Fast Refresh
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR@vitejs/plugin-react-swc\fP uses \fRSWC\fP for Fast Refresh
.PP
.SH "React Compiler"
.PP
The React Compiler is not enabled on this template because of its impact on dev & build performances\&. To add it, see \fRthis documentation\fP\&.
.SH "Expanding the ESLint configuration"
.PP
If you are developing a production application, we recommend updating the configuration to enable type-aware lint rules:

.PP
.PP
.nf
export default defineConfig([
  globalIgnores(['dist']),
  {
    files: ['**/*\&.{ts,tsx}'],
    extends: [
      // Other configs\&.\&.\&.

      // Remove tseslint\&.configs\&.recommended and replace with this
      tseslint\&.configs\&.recommendedTypeChecked,
      // Alternatively, use this for stricter rules
      tseslint\&.configs\&.strictTypeChecked,
      // Optionally, add this for stylistic rules
      tseslint\&.configs\&.stylisticTypeChecked,

      // Other configs\&.\&.\&.
    ],
    languageOptions: {
      parserOptions: {
        project: ['\&./tsconfig\&.node\&.json', '\&./tsconfig\&.app\&.json'],
        tsconfigRootDir: import\&.meta\&.dirname,
      },
      // other options\&.\&.\&.
    },
  },
])
.fi
.PP

.PP
You can also install \fReslint-plugin-react-x\fP and \fReslint-plugin-react-dom\fP for React-specific lint rules:

.PP
.PP
